ew addition of the road  color changing model which actually  allows you to remove the markings on  your highway and if you combine this  with culpable s fault and the movement  modes and all kinds of asset mods to  spice things up a little bit I think you  can actually make a core functioning  sort of underground programming for the  cars so that your junction is actually  going to be functioning and then just  make that all invisible and build the  entire look of the junction just out of  assets so I really just use the highway  pieces because that allows me to change  their color and also remove all of the  markings as the background of where the  cars are going to go but the rest is  really just going to filled  be filled quite a bit by probable s4 and  really just be made using custom lines  and assets just to get the exact touch  look it's also a bit of a bit of a I  guess a solution to the problem that  city skylines has inversely where you  don't get more lanes just blow off for  traffic lights which is very unfortunate  it's one of the things that I is really  one of my biggest gripes about the  traffic assuming game so that kind of  helps as well but it also just means  that you know whatever kind of details I  add to the junction to add that sort of  touch flair to it  the cars are still going to use this  Junction only problem is some of the  nodes are so close together and even  though I managed to fix the z-fighting  with the probable s4 pieces the cars  simply just don't really understand  what's going on here and there's a  similar case for the arrows because I  can't remove some of the arrows and I  also can't change their directions which  is which is a pretty big problem it's  not a very big problem I was able to  remove most of  but some are still pointing in different  directions than the part of the road is  going south quite unfortunate you'll  notice for instance that the top left  and bottom right arrows are pointing and  weird other directions but yeah so get  to the actual junction itself because  there's a lot of introduction that I  want to talk about here the general idea  for the junction is quite simple but  it's it's based on a very famous video  even at this point which is from the  view from the psychopath home blog which  is a really cool blog about cycling  infrastructure and they made a video  about Dutch chunking dutch junction  design in its like psycho friendly way  i'll post that in the description and it  has about 400,000 views and quite a bit  more and it's kind of well known it's  not the most well-known example of Dutch  Junction design if not for the fact that  it's not entirely touched problem with  the video is that it has been understood  quite a bit or misunderstood quite a bit  and also been applied in some wrong ways  it's not really a guide as to how to  make a Dutch Junction but it's  apparently from the creators of the blog  itself taken out of context since it's  really just an idea on the philosophies  behind that Junction design and a way to  turn a standard us Junction into  something that is more like the Dutch  protected Junction design which is lot  better for cyclists that said the entire  design of that Junction including the  very idea of having traffic lights and  protected Islands in the middle of the  traffic junction it's something that's  very old fashioned in the Netherlands  right now that's not to say that it  doesn't exist anymore it's just not that  common and many of these kinds of  interchanges are right now being removed  to be replaced by roundabouts which  handle more volume than a regular  intersection and they're also just more  safe so that's one thing to note about  this intersection I just really wanted  to try something like this and do it a  little bit different than that video  still applying some of the base  philosophies that make it a Dutch design  which I'll get into in a bit but at the  same time widening it up a little bit  because 